  "description": "The classic freestyle BMX formula: Front and rear brakes, a Gyro detangler and four pegs. The Leucadia DLX has it all. Whether you're getting serious about BMX or getting back into it after some time away, this is bike checks the boxes. A 20.5\" top tube has room to move, with 3-piece chromoly cranks and a sealed bottom bracket, 20 X 2.4\" La Mesa tires for max traction and Haro Team grips and a top load stem in the control center, you get everything you need to nail the tricks and make the feels real.\nHi-ten frame with 18.5\" or 20.5\" top tube\nFull hi-ten fork with tapered legs\nHi-ten bars 8.5\" with Haro 1978 alloy top load stem\nHaro Baseline 3-piece chromoly 8-spline 165mm (on 18.5\") or 170mm (on 20.3\") cranks with loose ball USA BB\n25/9 gearing with sealed bearing 9T driver\nHaro Baseline 48mm Forged stem\nHaro MS5 20X2.35 Tire\nHaro Team grips\nFour pegs, front 990 brakes and Gyro",
